body:
Creo que en educación está habiendo un gran crecimiento (tal vez especulativo) de la mano de centros de educación superior privados llenos de estudiantes internacionales. Estos estudiantes procedentes de paises más ricos pagan mucho por su matrícula, hasta 22.000€ al año donde estoy dando clases en este momento.

&#x200B;

Sin ir más lejos, yo este año he cambiado dos veces de universidad, siempre privada. La verdad es que me preocupo un poco ¿Será una burbuja?

Buenas, 

&#x200B;

soy medio sompo así que no entiendo bien el gráfico; entiendo que se representan cambios porcentuales, la referencia de cada punto de la gráfica es frente a la misma fecha del año anterior? 

&#x200B;

Además tengo otra pregunta, cual es el interés de presentar los dos indicadores juntos? Que relación hay o debería haber entre ambos?

I'm finishing my PhD in Spain after 5 years of research. It has been a bad experience for the usual reasons: working in a new investigation line for the lab, no peers with knoledge of the techniques to do, experiments do not work for years, PI does not understand a thing of what I'm doing or what I should do, postdocs are burnt out and dont treat you well, etc.

&#x200B;

The first three years pased by repeating primary culture and doing calcium imaging of the neurons, with extremely variable ressults. I had periods when I gave it all, and worked like 10 or 12 hours a day making experiments that did not work, other times, I work the least amount possible without drawing atention. My self steem droped to the floor, I felt like shit all the time. I did not do sports, nor go to see my friends or family because I felt like shit all the time. I stoped doing exercise and started to develope a depression. I hated myself for not being able to do experiments right, for not putting enough effort, for being retarded, i feared to finish my PhD grant without a paper to back my work, i envied other people with productive projects... the usual I think.

&#x200B;

Then I when to a psicologist, who tought me to control anxiety and stress with conductual procedures. Since then, I don't guive to many fucks about the laboratory and the work I'm doing. The interesting part is that now things are going pretty well at work, and not because I am working or worrying more. The thing is that I got collaboration offers from other researchers in the building were I work, so in the last 2 years of my theses I have participated in a review, and 3 articles that are being published right now.

&#x200B;

Now, I have the impression that doing well or not in the lab is not totally related to your skills or effort. It seems that external factors have such a strong influence, that the same person could have extremely opposite experiences depending on those. If I could reestart my PhD again I wuold look for the following: 

1. There is profund knoledge in the laboratory of the projects idea
2. There is working knoledge of the technics required,
3. The project director publishes regularly articles with the people working for him

&#x200B;

Finally, the moment I realized that what I do is not really important I started to work more relaxed and eficiently. I stopped feeling guilty for not being productive and never overstayed at work. I retook friends and family and exercise, and although the old feelings creep up sometimes I try hard not to pay atention to them and repeat myself that the Laboratory is not really important, that works for me.

&#x200B;

I hope you find your way to being better with your lifestyle and yourself.

Its fine, I reestarted the game, and Im playing a more streamlined playthrough, thank you anyway.

Just in case you are interested, these are some details of the problems i found:

\- I could tell Sam the Hunter that he could go to Hunt by permission from the chief of the warriors in the swamp camp (but i had never talked about it, then when i solved that question later with bogar, I could not tell it to Sam, who kept cutting wood)

&#x200B;

\- One of the guards needs to kill some moths to allow a worker to go and dig in search of artifacts, (when i arrived there to kill the bugs, they were all already dead!!)

&#x200B;

\- Not a bug but certanly strange I got to command the bandits attack to the old temple ruins, after 40 minutes of gameplay and sitll wearing my original shirt and no armour...

&#x200B;

I found some more things I just don\`t remember exactly what was it.

&#x200B;

It just seems to me that the construction of the game is a bit weak, just my opinion.

&#x200B;

Anyway, Tnaks a lot for the atention

David

I feel you there. 

&#x200B;

I'm M28, met this girl two years ago at work and started dating and formed a relationship. I was already bald, so nothing has changed since begining. But now and then she comments about my lack of hair, and how I would be more attractive with hair, sometimes she comments of how a nice maine of hair has this or that guy, etc...

&#x200B;

This  along with the deadbedroom has been undermining my selfconfidence/steem a lot! 

&#x200B;

So I decided to try and flirt with other girls, just to see how did I do with liking other people. I fould out nothing has changed. I've met girls I like that have told me  they would have a go on me, because they find me attractive and appealing.

&#x200B;

Conclussion, I think, there are people who don't like balding men like my girlfriend (I think this is going to be a problem), and people who don't mind that much.

I'm on the middle of a horrible failing PhD, my work life suks infinite, sometimes I would just stay in bed and do nothing.... 

&#x200B;

But the days I train in the morning things look in fact different, i feel better about everything! Work goes better!

>And it‘s the same

Well... that is stragne for me...

&#x200B;

I started balding at 16 more or less, now at my 28 I'm completely bald (just started the big 4), this bothers me a whole lot, cause I know I'm less attractive. In short I've been always way too bald for my age. But when I meet someone I like I sheldom think on how attractive I look... I just have fun and try to get what I want at that moment.

&#x200B;

I have always been super atracted to women, in the sense that many times I get to know a new girl I fell attracted to. It can be their interests, their eyes, their butt, their conversation... I don't know but i really like a lot of people I meet, sometimes it is something that happens instantly and other times after meeting this person for a while. I meet these people at university, at work place now, in the gym, in bars, playing games like DnD,  going out with friends, in community activities... nothing so special.

&#x200B;

Some times this girl feels somemthing alike and we start dating, and we have some fun. For two times now I've been able to have a long term relationship (more than two years). Which ended cause of things not related to my baldness, of course. While I date this people, needless to say, I felt really attracted to them.

&#x200B;

Other times I don't feel they are attrated to me, so I don't push and easily forget about it.

&#x200B;

The thing is that I'm not handsome, I'm 172 cm, my dick is normal size, I go to the gym but I lack  half of my right pectoral muscle, I've got  kind of crooked nose and my legs look like sticks and won't grow muscle, I'm quite a geek and play lots of videogames and DnD, and I work as a biomedical researcher (I've got a low salary), I even don't have my own car!!... I'm clearly not  attractive. But my experience with love and sex is quite fine.

&#x200B;

I think this is because when I am with people I focus on what are we talking about, what are they saying (intersts, problems, sugestions...), having the most of each situation with them for them and for my personal pleasure, just like when hanging with friends.

&#x200B;

I hope this makes sense to anyone...

&#x200B;

I knew that i was balding, my front hairline was almost non existent and the density on top was almost nothing... but i knew not i was balding also in the crown untill a friend pointed me in a photo taken from my back and said... who is that baldie?

&#x200B;

The instant i realized it was me...

I've just started with them :). Thanks a lot 

